name: _smoke_record
kind: structured_record (Tier-M predicate-grammar infrastructure smoke test)
source: SYNTHETIC -- fabricated by the author for this task, NOT a real
  security/financial/drug-safety/clinical-trial record. This directory holds
  no content files; it exists only so bench/validate.py's generic
  "artifact dir exists and contains PROVENANCE" check applies uniformly to
  every domain, including structured-record ones. The actual record data
  the runtime reads at run time is embedded verbatim in the instance JSON's
  top-level "records" field (bench/instances/_smoke_record/rec-0001.json),
  per the structured-record capability's offline-replayable design -- see
  prime_runtime/RECORD_ORACLE_REPORT.md.
purpose: Proves the generic structured-record oracle pipeline end-to-end
  (schema -> resolver -> goldledger -> oracle -> runner -> bench validator)
  before any of the four real record domains (security/OSV, financial/
  SEC-XBRL, drug-safety/openFDA, clinical-trials/CTgov) are authored on top
  of this infrastructure.
integrity: every field of every embedded record is authored plainly-labeled
  fiction (ids like "SMOKE-VULN-0001", a package name "acme-widget" that
  does not exist on any real package index, a URL under the reserved
  example.invalid TLD). No claim is ever made that this is real-world data.
exclusion: this instance (id rec-0001) and any run output under
  results/_smoke_record/ are excluded by path from analysis/aggregate.py
  and analysis/fill_paper.py so this synthetic instance can never leak into
  a paper table.
